#: ../../tools/dose_response_tools.rst:110 02e0733195fb4668837b63468cbdcd05
msgid ""
"Nonlinear regression of paired concentration-response measurements to the"
" Hill sigmoidal (4PL) mo..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/dose_response_tools.rst 19a709a7ea164af7b3f63671db6ca464
msgid "DoseResponse_fit_curve tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/dose_response_tools.rst:116 83a3978baa3b4435b78037a51dcf683e
msgid "**Name**: ``DoseResponse_fit_curve``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/dose_response_tools.rst:118 a3f37d4c9d26474a88e8ec41395c7ded
msgid ""
"**Description**: Nonlinear regression of paired concentration-response "
"measurements to the Hill sigmoidal (4PL) model: f(x) = Emin + (Emax - "
"Emin) / (1 + (EC50/x)^n). Returns the four fitted parameters (baseline "
"Emin, plateau Emax, midpoint EC50, Hill exponent n) with standard errors,"
" 95% CI for EC50, coefficient of determination R2, and predicted response"
" at each measured concentration. Requires at least 4 positive "
"concentration inputs. Useful for characterising pharmacological potency "
"and assessing assay data quality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/dose_response_tools.rst:125 d37de7852c024d7ca6e51520bcbc8e37
msgid ""
"``concentrations`` (array) (required) Drug concentrations (must be "
"positive, e.g., [0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100] in µM). At least 4 points "
"required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/dose_response_tools.rst:128 6c42725ae9a7489491960f03b43fc40c
#, python-format
msgid ""
"``responses`` (array) (required) Observed responses at each concentration"
" (e.g., % inhibition [0-100] or viability [0-100]). Same length as "
"concentrations."
msgstr ""

